{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: R9 items 1 to 4 (shared setting parsers and per-use readiness, truthful health 503 for configured unusable wiring, one DEPLOYMENT byte bound, and deploy:scope --keep-vars) at exact head 8087f038d44058011004d93cb519d96466589ff8, tree c415fe8d977aeb6e96614bb73ab55c02bd225d65 (review request e8aa5404, promise a14e189f; implementation requests 89cca717 with promise 7c0d93f2 and 5179f3a1 with promise 0cb892f3). This review binds both implementation requests to the one candidate. It may land. Deployment is planner-owned and carries the notes at the end.\n\nRead order: I read the primary, notes/implementation/2026-10-24-settings-readiness.md (artifact 7c48daab), first and in full, then the 28 supporting artifacts, then the sibling primary 6ad775f6 (the same note) and its two supports (docs/deploy.md and package.json). The worktree is clean at the head on branch builder/security-r9-settings-readiness-20261024. The merge-base with Main is Main itself, 55e4be6c; the head is 15 commits above it, including merges of the landed archive, bearer-expiry and diagnostic heads. The delta against Main is 29 files, 433 insertions and 82 deletions, and the act log holds a pointer at this head for every one of them. The gate head b3d9ad34 (tree bf2a345b) differs from the final head only in the implementation note, so gate 53493 carries without a repeat (docs/testing.md:597).\n\nConditions of 89cca717, each checked in source:\n1. Shared actual setting parsers: artifactsConfiguration and gitHubConfiguration are the single parsers; both now accept unknown, catch parse failures, and use the adapters' own predicates (artifactsService from artifacts-host.ts, gitHubPrivateKey from packages/git/src/github.ts), so the configuration check and the constructor agree. The namespace .git refusal matches the provider's repositoryName.\n2. Per-use readiness: artifactsReadiness and gitHubReadiness return wired with the parsed configuration and bindings, or off with one finite reason. The factory (artifactsOutside, gitHubOutside), the site reader (readerOf for both hosts) and health call the same functions. The site reader's private partial setting reader is deleted.\n3. Truthful health: health adds wiring.artifacts and wiring.github, each either {state wired} or {state off, reason}, and returns 503 when any configured host is off for a reason other than unconfigured, even with a ready register; ambiguous register roots still return 503; HEAD keeps the status with no body. No configuration contents, key, token or cleanup map is in the body; the test asserts the absence of every fixture secret.\n4. One DEPLOYMENT bound: readDeployment accepts a string of 1 to 128 UTF-8 bytes. Sessions, operational metrics, the hosted-agent metrics in worker.ts, demo creation (both config readers, tightened from 256 characters), parentless admission, child lineage, health and the application screen route use it. A configured invalid value refuses parentless admission even with ALLOW_OPEN_CREATION \"true\", makes child lineage unavailable before any ancestor lookup, makes the screen route answer 503 before any object or trust read, and gives metrics the fixed label unknown. An absent setting keeps its previous local behavior in every consumer. APPLICATION_TRUST and its parser are untouched.\n5. No provider calls, deployments or installs: readiness is syntax and shape only; the health and site tests bind provider stand-ins that fail the test if touched, and the readiness refusals make no request.\n\nConditions of 5179f3a1: package.json's deploy:scope now passes --keep-vars before --config; docs/deploy.md states the default command, the pinned scratch-directory Grow command, and that --keep-vars preserves plain settings the file omits without supplying or validating any value. No deployment is claimed.\n\nCode conclusions. The readiness order is deliberate: an undefined setting is the only path to unconfigured, so a present but malformed setting can never be mistaken for absence. gitHubReadiness checks the key, read, creation and cleanup settings with the same predicates the factory used before, so admission outcomes are unchanged and only the reason becomes visible; the site reader now requires full readiness, which is the requested tightening. The .git suffix and service-host checks in artifactsConfiguration move refusals the provider constructor already made into the parser, so no working live configuration becomes invalid. readDeployment is the one place the bound lives. The screen route resolves deployment before the try block and before trust is read, so an invalid value costs no Durable Object call. The seal file re-seals the eight touched owners; the seal test run once at the head passes 4 of 4, which computes the parser values for every sealed file.\n\nEvidence verified. Gate 53493 raw at b3d9ad34: expectedHead and expectedTree as recorded, unchanged checkpoint, gatePassed, before and after equal, eight stages exit 0, Node 39 of 39 and Counting 55 of 55; the independent audit (manifest 4 files, every sha256 verified) records 3,551 terminal rows with 3,548 passed and 3 skipped across 498 files, 0 unhandled errors, and complete callbacks for all 47 R9 cases across the 13 changed test files. Controls: the optional-credential control disabled the creation-token refusal in github-wiring.ts (original digest equals the head's file, needle present) and left github-wiring.test.ts:170:41 red with the other case passing; the deployment-utf8 control removed the byte bound in deployment-setting.ts (original digest equals the head's file, needle present) and left sessions.test.ts:261:114 red with its other two cases passing; both children exited 1, both before and after checkpoints are identical. The earlier affected run 72848 (47 assertions) and its wrapper failure are retained as history and not relied on here.\n\nDocument checks at 8087f038:\n- git diff --check from Main 55e4be6c is clean;\n- check-commit-messages from 55e4be6c reports 15 checked, 0 flagged; the longest subject is 74 characters;\n- section citations on an export report 1,877 resolved, 0 broken and 5 known unresolved; the citation script is identical to Main's;\n- merging the head into Main 55e4be6c gives exactly its tree, c415fe8d;\n- docs/deploy.md's new statements are true at this head; the implementation note's \"exact-head review, landing and deployment remain pending\" is its dated report form, accepted as for the other heads today.\n\nArchitecture: one parser per host setting, one readiness function per host, one deployment bound, each used by every consumer; health reports the same admission the factory makes instead of a parallel approximation. The deleted site-side partial reader removes the last divergent copy. This is the right shape for R9 and leaves R10 and R11 as separate policy work.\n\nSecurity: the reasons on public /health are a finite enumeration with no values, so a caller learns which host settings are present and which class is malformed, which is the operational truth the request asked for and leaks no secret; register scopes stay out of the body. Invalid DEPLOYMENT now fails closed everywhere instead of opening local creation or becoming an unbounded metrics label. Readiness is recomputed per health call from settings the operator controls (at most 4 KiB per configuration, 16 KiB key, 1 MiB cleanup map), which is bounded and acceptable; no new entry point, provider call or secret handling is introduced.\n\nSimplification: nonblocking. Seven files gain the readDeployment import above their file header comment, which puts the import before the file's description; harmless. The site reader keeps a redundant read-token check that readiness already guarantees. Readiness could be memoized per isolate if /health traffic ever matters; not needed now.\n\nWorkroom note, not a defect of the head: the note, docs/deploy.md and package.json each have two artifact events at this one head, one per implementation request. Prepare accepted all 32 and both bindings; the merge's retirement trailers should be checked for both events of each pair.\n\nResidual notes for the planner's deploy: after deploying, /health on any Worker whose configured host cannot wire will return 503 with the reason; that is the new truthful signal, so correct or remove that setting rather than treating it as an outage. --keep-vars preserves settings absent from the file; reviewed --var values for dap-grow still have to be passed on the same command. Hosted MCP stays closed unless MCP_ENABLED is set in the same step (10f45efc). Nothing is deployed or claimed deployed by this head.\n\nFindings: none blocking.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7c48daab3fbd95604eaebc2be25e6d4a04651e7c","binding":"assigned","head":"8087f038d44058011004d93cb519d96466589ff8","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a14e189fc50aaa64bcb18fb73ceb3bb7d021f040\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7c0d93f2a5b5f6f6c25fc33a048f37c87c9150dd\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0cb892f384e32872f19b555f100c5fa37bcff226\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5468ea19a1815cf0d636689e4bf632b2b566d508","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}